course: dictionary
lesson: 2009
title: Gas, cooling and water drops
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Condensation happens when a gas cools down and turns into a liquid. The gas we mean is usually water vapour, which is water in the air as an invisible gas. «Condensation is a gas turning into a liquid when it cools.»
explain: Think about a cold drink can on a warm day. The air near the can holds water vapour. The can is cold, so the vapour cools, turns back into liquid, and tiny drops appear on the outside. That is condensation, and it is why the can looks wet.
explain: Condensation is also the name for the drops themselves. «The window was covered in condensation» means the tiny drops of water on the glass.
fact: Condensation is when a gas cools and turns into a liquid.
fact: Water vapour is water in the form of a gas. You cannot see it.
fact: Condensation also means the little drops of water that form on a cold surface, like a window or a cold glass.
fact: In the water cycle, condensation is the step where water vapour turns back into liquid and makes clouds and dew.
fact: «Water dripping from a recorder is condensation.» Warm, wet breath cools inside the pipe and turns back into drops.
exercise: What does condensation mean? | A very high cloud in the sky | Rain falling from a cloud | A liquid turning into a gas when it gets hot | * A gas cooling down and turning into a liquid
exercise: «The window was covered in condensation.» What is the condensation? | A gas that has been heated up | A cloud that has come inside | Dry dust from the room | * Tiny drops of water on the cold glass
exercise: «Condensation is a gas turning into a liquid when it cools.» Which word tells you what the gas turns into? | condensation | gas | cools | * liquid
test: Why do drops form on the outside of a cold can on a warm day? | The can is melting in the sun | * Water vapour in the warm air cools and turns into liquid | It is raining inside the room | The can is making water inside itself
test: «Water dripping from a recorder is condensation.» Why is this condensation? | Any dripping thing is condensation | Breath is a solid, so it drips | The recorder is made of water | * Warm, wet breath cools inside the pipe and turns back into drops
exam: In «Condensation is a gas turning into a liquid when it cools», what happens when the gas cools? | It disappears for ever | It becomes hotter and lighter | * It turns into a liquid | It turns into solid ice straight away
